<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Amurru</h1><p class="st-meta">1400 BCE – 1190 BCE (approx.) · capital Sumur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Amurru, a kingdom on the Syrian-Lebanese coast built by adventurers in the Amarna age, which changed sides between Egypt and the Hittites.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Amurru was the mountainous land behind the coast between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byblos">Byblos</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ugarit">Ugarit</a>, home to fugitives and landless groups. In the 14th century BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdi-ashirta">Abdi-Ashirta</a> united them into a kingdom at the expense of Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aziru">Aziru</a> captured <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/simyra">Simyra</a> and made it his capital, despite angry letters from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rib-hadda">Rib-Hadda</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byblos">Byblos</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aziru">Aziru</a> defected from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/egyptian-empire-new-kingdom">Egyptian Empire New Kingdom</a> to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> and signed a treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suppiluliuma-i">Suppiluliuma I</a>. His successors ruled as Hittite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> with family ties to the Hittite court; a treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaushgamuwa">Shaushgamuwa</a> ordered him to stop Ahhiyawan ships from trading with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benteshina">Bentesina</a> was deposed for siding with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> after <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kadesh">Kadesh</a> but restored by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusili-iii">Hattusili III</a>. Around 1190 BCE Amurru was overrun in the attacks by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-peoples">Sea Peoples</a> recorded at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medinet-habu">Medinet Habu</a>, and the kingdom disappeared.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1400 BCE – 1190 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:31.84%;width:4.18%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1400 BCE – 1190 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century-bce">15th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sumur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdi-Ashirta, Aziru, Shaushgamuwa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Canaanite religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Akkadian, Canaanite</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/lebanon">Lebanon</a>, <a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Amurru</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1295&amp;focus=kingdom-of-amurru" aria-label="Kingdom of Amurru on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5592 944 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Amurru lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5863 1489h0M5852 1002h0M5914 1177h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5912 1200h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5912 1200h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Lebanon. <a href="/atlas?year=-1295&amp;focus=kingdom-of-amurru">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

